  "how does he know the retrieval is actually working?": {
    "answer": "He checks the retrieval by measuring latency and comparing it to the exhaustive scan. The exhaustive in-memory scan takes 0.5 to 2.9 milliseconds, while the database takes 46 to 198 milliseconds, which is 30 to 380 times longer for the same top result. Both need the query embedding first, so that cost is excluded from both sides. He also runs 112 structural checks and 25 evaluation cases five times each to verify correctness. The retrieval serves from an index bundled with the function, not from the vector database, because the measurement shows the bundled index is significantly faster.",
